  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Assessment of Macroeconomic benefits of Net Zero and Climate Resilient Pathways</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Under the Paris Agreement, the Parties are expected to develop and communicate their NDCs every 5 years, gradually increasing their ambition towards achieving the target to limit the increase in global average temperature to well below 2&#xB0;C and to pursue efforts to limit the increase to 1.5&#xB0;C. The NDCs contain information on climate change actions, technologies, ambition targets, and needs for the provision of finance and capacity building. Understanding and assessing the socio-economic and macroeconomic benefits and investment needs of low-carbon and climate-resilient pathways of countries&#x2019; NDCs would provide essential information for supporting and catalyzing climate action. The macroeconomic assessment of countries&#x2019; NDCs will illustrate the opportunities for leapfrogging and transitioning to a zero-carbon and climate-resilient development path.</narrative>
  </description>
